  Version 0.47.0
  (2026-07-31) continued the v3 backfill with Academy of Management Journal
  volume 64 issue 5 and volume 64 issue 4 — 25 notes, all v2 augmentations.
  A backfill adds no papers, so the record total is unchanged at 1,167; the
  version-tier census shifts to 61 v1, 759 v2, and 347 v3 notes. The upgrade
  phase was the fourth consecutive clean one, with 24 of 25 augmentations
  passing the validator and the mechanical diff-guard on the first attempt.
  Each touched note passed a fresh full independent 9-field rubric-v2 audit at
  224 of 225 prose-field verdicts SUPPORTED, after seven evidence-based repairs
  across six notes in three repair rounds. All six round-1 PARTIAL verdicts fell
  on legacy prose fields written before the v3 standard and none on the three new
  v3 sections, the cleanest new-field result of the backfill so far. One PARTIAL
  is accepted and documented rather than edited: Sitzmann's Future Research is
  the interleaved-references truncation class, where the REFERENCES heading sits
  atop the second column while the first still carries body prose, so the strip
  discarded 24.6% of the paper and the flagged claim verifies in the raw text.
  A seventh repair came not from the audit but from an augmentation agent's
